sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Trigger as Admin or generation worker
  participant Service as Payout service
  participant DB as MySQL
  participant Processor as Admin or processing worker
  participant Stripe as Stripe
  participant Recovery as Recovery worker
  Trigger->>Service: Generate eligible payouts
  Service->>DB: Find paid bookings past checkout hold
  DB-->>Service: Eligible bookings
  Service->>Service: Group by hotel, owner and currency
  Service->>DB: Check ready account and available balance
  Service->>DB: Atomically create pending payout and booking items
  Processor->>Service: Process payout
  Service->>DB: Lock balance and payout, then recheck funds
  Service->>DB: Set processing
  Service->>Stripe: Create transfer with key payout-ID
  alt Transfer response received
    Stripe-->>Service: Transfer ID
    Service->>DB: Atomically commit ledger settlement and paid status
  else Definitive rejection
    Stripe-->>Service: Rejected request
    Service->>DB: Set failed
  else Timeout or uncertain outcome
    Service->>DB: Keep processing and save error
    Recovery->>Service: Resume stale payout
    Service->>Stripe: Retrieve known transfer or replay original key
    Stripe-->>Service: Transfer result
    alt Transfer confirmed
      Service->>DB: Commit ledger settlement and paid status
    else Still uncertain
      Service->>DB: Keep processing for later reconciliation
    else Definitive failure
      Service->>DB: Set failed
    end
  end
